        <!-- ======================= /our-club ======================= -->
        <template id="page_our_club_view" name="Our Club">
            <t t-call="website.layout">
                <div id="wrap" class="oe_structure">
                    <section class="pt32 pb16">
                        <div class="container">
                            <h1>Our Club</h1>
                            <h2>About SCRA</h2>
                            <p>SCRA's mission centers on fostering enthusiasm for amateur radio,
                            electronics technology, and associated disciplines. The club
                            accomplishes this through monthly meetings featuring relevant
                            topics, communication assistance for local events, emergency
                            preparedness education, and maintenance of community repeater
                            infrastructure.</p>

                            <h3>Membership</h3>
                            <p>Membership welcomes all individuals with an interest in amateur
                            radio, regardless of licensing status. Annual dues are $20 per
                            person, with reduced rates available for families and members
                            under 24 years old.</p>
                            <p><strong>Member benefits include:</strong></p>
                            <ul>
                                <li>Access to loaner equipment - handhelds through HF base
                                stations, antennas, test gear, and complete portable SOTA/POTA
                                setups</li>
                                <li>Exclusive tours and activities - mini-DXpeditions, historical
                                radio site visits, NASA Ames Research Center access</li>
                                <li>The monthly Short Skip newsletter with articles and industry
                                news</li>
                            </ul>
                            <p><a href="/store">Join today</a></p>

                            <h3>Meetings</h3>
                            <p>SCRA meetings take place at 7pm on the first Wednesday of each
                            month at the Luther Burbank Art and Garden Center, 2050 Yulupa
                            Avenue in Santa Rosa. Admission is free and open to the public.</p>
                            <p><a href="/our-club/meetings">More about meetings</a></p>

                            <h3>Education</h3>
                            <p>The club offers diverse instructional programs: Technician
                            license preparation, General and Extra level study sessions, Morse
                            code instruction, and kit and station assembly courses.</p>
                            <p><a href="/events/classes">Technician License Class</a></p>

                            <h3>Community Service</h3>
                            <p>Volunteer initiatives encompass event communications support,
                            public demonstrations, and disaster preparedness coordination.</p>
                            <p><a href="/events/public-service">Public Service</a></p>

                            <h3>Field Day</h3>
                            <p>This annual 24-hour national event challenges operators to
                            maximize contacts while simulating emergency conditions using
                            generators and renewable power sources, during the fourth full
                            weekend in June.</p>
                            <p><a href="/events/field-day">Field Day details</a></p>

                            <hr/>
                            <p><strong>Sonoma County Radio Amateurs, Inc.</strong><br/>
                            501(c)(3) nonprofit, Federal ID 68-0005765<br/>
                            PO Box 116, Santa Rosa CA 95402-0116<br/>
                            <a href="/donate">Donate</a></p>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                </div>
            </t>
        </template>
        <record id="page_our_club" model="website.page">
            <field name="url">/our-club</field>
            <field name="is_published">True</field>
            <field name="view_id" ref="page_our_club_view" />
        </record>

        <!-- ================= /our-club/meetings ================= -->
        <template id="page_our_club_meetings_view" name="Meetings">
            <t t-call="website.layout">
                <div id="wrap" class="oe_structure">
                    <section class="pt32 pb16">
                        <div class="container">
                            <h1>Meetings</h1>
                            <p>SCRA welcomes members and guests to hybrid monthly membership
                            meetings. Each gathering features a presentation or activity
                            announced via the club's newsletter and calendar.</p>

                            <h3>Meeting Format</h3>
                            <ul>
                                <li><strong>Online via Zoom</strong> - meetings occur at 7:00pm
                                on the first Wednesday of each month. Send an email to the SCRA
                                president at
                                <a href="mailto:k6son@arrl.net">k6son@arrl.net</a> with "Zoom MM
                                request" in the subject line.</li>
                                <li><strong>In-Person</strong> - arrive at 6:30pm for social time
                                and light refreshments; the official start time is 7:00pm.</li>
                            </ul>

                            <h3>Location</h3>
                            <p><strong>Luther Burbank Art &amp; Garden Center</strong><br/>
                            2050 Yulupa Avenue<br/>
                            Santa Rosa, CA</p>
                            <p><em>Not the Luther Burbank Gardens on Sonoma Ave or the Luther
                            Burbank Center on River Road!</em></p>

                            <h3>Special Scheduling Notes</h3>
                            <p>December meetings are replaced with a Holiday Party for members.
                            When the first Wednesday falls on a major holiday (such as New
                            Year's Day), the meeting moves to the first Thursday of that month
                            instead.</p>
                        </div>
                    </section>
                </div>
            </t>
        </template>
